{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: a bare piece size in a parenthetical (\"(approximately 2-inch pieces)\") becomes a \"1 2-inch pieces\" alternative",
  "description": "\"1 cup lightly-packed torn green leaf lettuce (approximately 2-inch pieces)\" gets an alternative measurement {amount: 1, unit: \"2-inch pieces\"}: try_parse_parenthetical_measurement recovers a hyphenated size unit and implies a count of 1. \
That sizes the pieces, it doesn't measure the whole, so it shouldn't be an alternative (and it's nonsense next to \"1 cup\"). \
The same happens without a prep word (\"(about 2-inch pieces)\"). \"(~1-inch piece)\" on \"30 grams fresh ginger\" is arguably a real alternative (one piece of ginger), so the fix probably needs to distinguish a plural \"pieces\" (a cut size) from a single \"piece\"/\"knob\" (a quantity). \
Rerun make pipeline; expect data/ diffs removing a handful of alternatives.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "bug",
